cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The AI Agent Engineering & Development Framework:
  The 10 Pillars of Production Agent Engineering
message: "If you use or reference this framework, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Vijay Prakash
    family-names: Tiwari
version: "1.2"
date-released: "2026-06-10"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A practitioner framework that reframes production AI agents as a
  systems-engineering problem organized around ten coordinated disciplines:
  Prompt, Goal, Trajectory, Context, Memory, Tool, Intelligence, Execution,
  Governance, and Evaluation Engineering. Includes three worked case studies,
  a six-phase development lifecycle, a CI/CD-for-agents model, a dual-evaluation
  principle, and a production readiness rubric, synthesizing peer-reviewed
  research with industry guidance and governance standards.
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent engineering
  - LLM
  - production AI
  - agent evaluation
  - AI governance
